# THE SINGLE SOURCE of the openwrt/luci commit this package borrows two BUILD TOOLS from, and of
# their checksums. Sourced as shell (`. luci-upstream.pin`) by update-po.sh and by tools/t0.sh.
#
# Both are downloaded over the network and then EXECUTED as gates, so a moving branch would make
# the gate whatever upstream pushed last:
#
#   jsmin.c        compiled, then run over every module and the OUTPUT re-parsed. jsmin's
#                  regex-vs-division lookback can eat the rest of a file and still EXIT 0, which
#                  is why the gate is a round-trip and not a grep for the pattern.
#   i18n-scan.pl   run by perl; decides whether the translation catalogue is complete.
#
# The pin matches luci-theme-footstrap's. That is deliberate rather than incidental: this package
# is checked with the same two linters as the theme it plugs into, and two companion projects
# disagreeing about which jsmin decides their JS is safe would be a difference nobody would look
# for. Bump them together.
#
# To bump: change LUCI_PIN, re-fetch both files at the new commit, update their sha256s. The
# sha256 is what actually holds the content — the commit only says which file to fetch.
LUCI_PIN=5cf20c5741dc34eea0faaf7324ef3751b05fa1f3
JSMIN_SHA256=0568b14873f27f339cf66a9c43603d0bc8ca501ff62522ea924c6e8daf1be215
I18N_SCAN_SHA256=a1823d1fdd942f31a105e1e53b401e146bc10527f231e016930b1a5123ef21d3
